You might have to wait a long time while being harassed by the curse of
ancient Yendor.  Rodney decides to intervene() every 200-249 turns (or
is it 50-249? I can't remember the order of the arguments to rn1()),
whereupon he will do one of the following things:

1/3 of the time: You feel vaguely nervous.
1/6 of the time: A random number (for most characters at this point, 1d3)
of cursings will be applied to random objects in your pack.
1/6 of the time: Aggravate monsters.
1/6 of the time: Summon nasties.
1/6 of the time: Materialise and attack you.

So, to get Rodney to appear, you're looking at possibly spending several
hundred turns waiting.  It does not take several hundred turns to get to
the High Priest.
